<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ghazni</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ghazni is a city in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> on the road between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandahar">Kandahar</a>. From 977 it was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghaznavid-empire">Ghaznavid Empire</a>, whose ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a> filled it with palaces, mosques and the spoils of his Indian raids, making it a centre of Persian culture. The Ghurids sacked it in 1150 and later ruled from it; two Ghaznavid minarets still stand.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ghazni.jpg" alt="Ghazni" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: US State Department (US Embassy in Kabul) a US Government organization, hence PD-USGov applies · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Citadel_of_Ghazni,_seen_from_Tapa_Sardar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
